Boeing B-52 Stratofortress for PteroSim

Flight dynamics

Lee Elliott's FlightGear B-52F YASim configuration is distributed under the
GNU General Public License, version 2 or later. The original XML and licence
are in source/. The JSBSim adaptation is distributed under the same licence.
https://github.com/FGMEMBERS/B-52F/blob/344df48dcb8231742615ef5f17bfb5a24b06f9cf/B-52F-yasim.xml

The adaptation uses the source's wing geometry and incidence, empty weight,
engine positions and dry thrust, fuel tank positions and capacities, and
tandem undercarriage geometry. The JSBSim aerodynamic coefficients, inertia,
damper and spring rates, and thrust lapse are estimates. The default tank
fill is 40%. Landing gear, flaps and brakes respond to JSBSim properties.
The Manual stick pilot drives roll, pitch, yaw and all eight throttles.
The PX4 SITL profile in firmwares/px4_B52 uses one motor output for all eight
turbines and separate outputs for elevator, aileron, rudder, flaps,
wheel brakes and ground steering.

Visual

Lee Elliott's FlightGear B-52F mesh (B-52F-002-027e.ac) and livery
(B-52F-02.rgb) are adapted from FlightGear FGAddon. The adapted model is
distributed under the GNU General Public License, version 2 or later.
https://svn.code.sf.net/p/flightgear/fgaddon/trunk/Aircraft/B-52F/Models/

The editable Blender source with packed livery is in source/flightgear-b52f.blend.
Its Airframe, LWingAileron and RWingAileron collections export separately as
Y-up binary glTF files. The conversion aligns the geometry to the JSBSim model
datum and omits the drag chute. The ailerons follow the corresponding JSBSim
roll control outputs. The remaining mesh is fixed, including the landing gear.
